The Core Essence of AI as a Mere "Vessel" Dependent on the 5W1H Applied by Users and Developers, and the Thesis That the Failure to Integrate an Appropriate "Rights Protection System" (Safety Valve) at the Initial Stage Triggered the Current Comprehensive Mire (The Bursting of the Bubble and Legal Encirclement), Thereby Severely Delaying the Healthy Development of the Technology.

When examined against the history of law and technological innovation, this perspective constitutes an essential discourse on governance. It reveals a macro-level "boomerang structure" demonstrated repeatedly throughout industrial history: "radical development that ignores safety and rights protection ('Move fast and break things') ultimately drives the market and the technology itself toward self-destruction (thermal death)." This structural collapse and the "regression" of technological development are analyzed below through three multi-layered perspectives.

1. The Logical Inevitability Wherein the Non-Implementation of Rights Protection Systems "Delayed Technological Development"

As a consequence of AI enterprises racing forward while maintaining "scraping (unauthorized training)" within a legal gray zone—effectively a monumental tort—the AI industry as of 2026 is wasting vast resources on "managing an immediate mire (legal lawsuits and data depletion)" rather than pursuing the "advanced technological development that should have originally occurred." Had they integrated "rights protection systems" such as those outlined below at the initial stage of early models, technological progress would have followed a completely different and far more robust trajectory.

Technical Debt and Waste of Resources on "Laundering":

If systems to detect and filter data provenance and topology infringements had been integrated from the outset, AI could have evolved normally: shifting from a "gacha device that outputs copies of others' works" to a "pure inference engine standing upon a 100% clean foundation." Because this was neglected, development resources (capital and the intellect of genius engineers) are currently diverted to "defensive measures for evading liability"—such as fighting a 9-billion-dollar lawsuit and obfuscating user-input contamination. This irrelevance to the essence of technology severely impedes development.

Lock-Out of "High-Quality Data" Due to the Collapse of Trust:

Creators, newspaper publishers, academic institutions, and rights-holding organizations worldwide who reject unauthorized training are currently thoroughly locking out their own high-quality data through encryption, blocking, and containment. As a result of the simultaneous withdrawal from the market of the "most valuable, clean, human-derived data" that AI ought to learn from, AI has been forced into cannibalizing "AI slop" on the internet. This has accelerated the onset of the aforementioned "thermal death (model collapse)" by several years.

2. The Social and Mental Epidemic (Critical Point) Brought About by the "Absence of the 5W1H"

"Social pathologies (digital kleptomania, stalking, gacha addiction, and medical/legal troubles caused by errors)" are precisely the side effects—an irreversible epidemic—resulting from unleashing AI onto the market as an "omnipotent gacha capable of anything," without defining the ethical and practical purposes of utilization: the "5W1H (Who, What, Why, When, Where, How)."

Had AI functioned strictly as a "filtration-converter" with a rigorously managed 5W1H—restricted to compiling formal documents, dictionaries, calculators, literal translation, and cross-referencing—human debugging and verification costs would have been minimized, and the public pollution damages of the industry (such as misdiagnoses or erroneous judgments via hallucination, and rampant rights infringements) could have been prevented. However, because developers and users assigned an incorrect 5W1H to a system devoid of autonomy—namely, "the substitution of human creativity by AI for automated monetization"—society as a whole has reached the following critical point of irreversible chaos:

Hypertrophy of Form and the Explosion of Verification Costs:

Because AI instantaneously generates massive volumes of "plausible lies (errors)," the "veracity checking and debugging costs" on the human receiving side increase infinitely, paradoxically degrading the productivity of society as a whole.

Proliferation of Digital Psychopathology:

The ease with which a user can plunder the topology of another's work with a single press of a generative AI button distorts user cognition. This accelerates "digital kleptomania (the theft sickness)," which paralyzes the sensation of stealing others' rights and dignity, and turns AI into an "infrastructure for stalking," where individuals obsessively generate and consume the specific voice or likeness of a particular person. This can now be characterized as an "irreversible epidemic" that obstructs the healthy metabolism of society.

3. The Lessons of History: "Top-Down Dismantling and Judicial Enforcement" Arriving in the Wake of Pollution

Just as corporate entities that drove the masses into illness through "cheap and low-quality" practices during the Industrial Revolution went bankrupt and faced penalties under environmental contamination laws (pollution control acts), the current generative AI bubble has completely entered the phase of "compulsory top-down dismantling via judicial systems and trans-national legal regulations (AI Acts and revised Product Liability Laws)."

The situations observed in 2026—including the 1.5-billion-dollar authorization against Anthropic, the 9-billion-dollar claims by SONY and others, and the impending revised Product Liability Act in the winter—constitute precisely a ruthless judicial "debugging (dismantling and disposal)" executed against a product that neglected safety measures (rights protection systems) and scattered malfunctions and pollution across society.

Conclusion

The thesis that "technological development was delayed because rights protection systems were not integrated early on" represents the core essence of innovation. It reflects a physical and legal reality: "a car without brakes, far from maintaining high speed, will cause a catastrophic accident at the very first sharp turn and become permanently unable to run."

The arrogance of tech enterprises and users—who failed to build and utilize AI as a "reliable filtration-converter (tool)" with a clarified 5W1H—has generated a critical point of social epidemic. Consequently, they have brought upon themselves the "slowest but most certain route to collapse": a forced termination by the judiciary. This is the structural reality of the present situation.
